        }
      ],
      "message": "test: make fill_mempool independent of malloc overhead\n\nfill_mempool() relied on exactly 72 of its ~67 kvB transactions fitting\nin a 5 MB mempool, and 75 not fitting, which only holds while each one\ncosts between 66.7 kB and 69.4 kB of mempool memory. That depends on\nhow much memory the platform's malloc uses for the 67443-byte output\nscript of each. Instead, keep sending transactions while two more would\nstill fit, judging by the mempool usage that the last one added.\n\nSimilarly, mempool_limit.py checked that transactions are large enough\nto trigger eviction by comparing their vsize against the maximum\nmempool usage minus the total vsize of the mempool. Compare against the\nremaining mempool usage instead: the usage of these transactions is at\nleast their vsize, as they are padded with output script data.",
